[Applause]  [Music]  the icy cold of January is about to get  defrosted with a bunch of nostalgia this  week's new releases feature all sorts of  retro inspired games cutesy creatures  and a bit of anime let's get to it  Nintendo is taking another step into the  mobile gaming world with Fire Emblem  heroes the tactic series has been shrunk  down to run on your smartphone but the  rock paper scissor style combat is still  fully intact this time around you play  as a summoner who must save the kingdom  of Oscar from being conquered and to do  this you'll have to summon heroes from  all across the Fire Emblem universe that  means you'll be commanding characters  from last year's Fire Emblem fates all  the way back to the original NES release  Fire Emblem heroes comes to iOS and  Android on Thursday februari second  double dragon four is not the fourth  game in the series but that's not the  important part what you need to know is  that it picks up after Double Dragon 2  and sees billy and jimmy beating up a  bunch of new enemies maybe those street  thugs are just misunderstood in any case  you can totally play through the whole  thing with a friend beyond the story you  can fight your way through tower mode by  taking on waves of enemies or turn co-op  in the competition with the new duel  mode Double Dragon four blasts its way  onto ps4 on january twenty ninth and  onto pc on the 30th we have a review on  the way too so be sure to check back  later if you're not sure about picking  it up if you prefer to let monsters do  the fighting for you then you might be  into digimon world next order the latest  in the digital monsters series sees you  raising two digimon at once which means  twice the training and combat strategies  they can fight on their own or listen to  any commands you give during battle  which never seems to work with my cat  you can play as either a male or female  student and you'll run into over 200  digimon that can be recruited into  joining and expanding your village  digimon world next  order was released on the Vita in Japan  last year but it's coming stateside to  the ps4 on January 31st are you feeling  nostalgic for the good old fashioned  game boy warlocks tower has got you  covered but don't let the cutesy tile  set fool you this puzzle game is not  easy every step taken is one life lost  which means you have a limited number of  moves to get through over 100 rooms  they're filled with zombies slimes  conveyor belts blocks and all sorts of  things that just want to get in your way  luckily you can play tag team style with  a buddy so at least you'll get a  breather between puzzles warlocks tower  comes to pc on january thirty first  speaking of cutesy games Poochie &amp;  Yoshi's woolly world is being shrunk  down for the 3ds the portable port has  everything from the Wii U game plus new  features like Poochie dash mode secret  Poochie pups and a scrapbook theater you  can still tap a Yoshi meebo to play as  double Yoshi in the game but the new  yarn pucci amoeba also adds new features  tap it in any main level and Yoshi will  ride his adorable dog tap it in one of  the bonus pucci stages to play in time  attack mode if you're in the mood for a  super cute platformer check out Poochie  &amp; Yoshi's woolly world when it hits 3ds  on februari third and those are the big  games will be playing this week as  always remember that release dates are  based on retailer listings and are  subject to change and don't forget to  subscribe to keep up with all the  hottest new releases every week thanks  for watching guys I'll see you next time  you  [Music]

